Platos
======

Platos is an open-source agent runtime platform maintained by Winsen Labs.

Platos is built on top of, and incorporates code from, the trigger.dev project.
The repository root LICENSE is the Apache License, Version 2.0. At the reviewed
upstream v4.4.4/5ea36e08 source anchor, trigger.dev's root LICENSE is also
Apache-2.0, while the public @trigger.dev/core package and private
@trigger.dev/otlp-importer package each declare MIT and carry a package-level
MIT LICENSE. Those root and package facts are distinct. The tag-to-commit
mapping is an externally reviewed point-in-time fact, not an offline-verified
live ref assertion.

  (The current public @platos/core manifest and package LICENSE are Apache-2.0.
  The private @platos/otlp-importer manifest and package LICENSE preserve the
  inherited upstream MIT metadata and bytes.

  Owner decision, 2026-09-01: Platos distributes @platos/core under Apache-2.0,
  and the upstream MIT permission notice is retained verbatim in
  packages/core/NOTICE under an explicit UPSTREAM ATTRIBUTION heading, published
  in the package tarball. MIT grants the right to sublicense, so the Apache-2.0
  distribution stands; the retained notice satisfies MIT's requirement that the
  copyright and permission notice accompany copies and substantial portions.
  It lives in NOTICE rather than LICENSE because every publishable package's
  LICENSE must stay byte-identical to the repository Apache-2.0 text, and
  NOTICE is the Apache-2.0 section 4(d) mechanism for exactly this. Retaining
  the notice makes the question moot rather than answering it in the abstract.

  See docs/audits/sbom/licence-resolution.json for the canonical offline
  provenance receipt and docs/audits/sbom/licence-resolution.md for its human
  summary and the recorded decision. The checked production closure is recorded in
  docs/audits/sbom/closure-contract.md and
  docs/audits/sbom/closure-receipts.json.)

